# Publish & live deploy (Loot & Lasers)

## Never push to the GitHub remote

- **Do not** run `git push`, `git push origin`, or any publish to github.com.
- The user’s partner owns the GitHub remote. This machine does **not** need to push upstream.
- **GitHub Desktop** on this PC shows the **local** git repo. A local `git commit` is what updates that Desktop view. That is the only “repo update” this agent performs for Desktop.

## “Commit and push” means (agent-driven, no GitHub remote)

When the user says **commit and push** (or equivalent), do **all** of the following:

1. **Commit locally** per `git-commit-convention.mdc` (milestone commits; no secrets).  
   → This is the GitHub Desktop repository update.
2. **Deploy Hetzner Node API** — run `scripts/deploy-hetzner-node-api.ps1` from the local checkout (SSH identity typically `C:\Users\Caide\Desktop\Stuff\Loot and lasers\SSH\Farts`).
3. **Deploy / reload Nakama** on staging — keep modules current; recreate/reload Nakama as needed (no game-data wipe). See `docs/STAGING_NAKAMA.md` / host compose.
4. **Never** build a Windows installer / Godot export unless the user **explicitly** asks for one.
5. **Never** push to `origin` / GitHub.com.

## Targets

| Target | On “commit and push” | Who |
|--------|----------------------|-----|
| **Local repo / GitHub Desktop** | Yes — `git commit` only | Agent |
| **GitHub.com remote** | **No** — partner’s workflow | Partner |
| **Hetzner Node API** | Yes — deploy | Agent |
| **Nakama** | Yes — reload/deploy | Agent |
| **Godot installer** | Only if asked | Agent when requested |

## Do not

- Ask the user to Push origin in Desktop (unless they explicitly want to sync for their partner).
- Attempt CLI or Desktop automation that publishes to github.com.
- Skip Hetzner/Nakama when they said commit and push (those are the live targets that matter here).
